## Pronoun stance
<e.g. "You" for the reader; "we" for the brand; never "I".>

## Lexical rules
- **Contractions**: <none | partial | full>
- **Sentence ceiling**: <max words per sentence; vary length>
- **Paragraph ceiling**: <max words per paragraph>
- **Summary label**: <e.g. "Quick answer">

## Headline patterns
- **Favor**: <question headlines / outcome + specificity / real numbers>
- **Avoid**: <clickbait / hype / "Ultimate Guide" filler / fake urgency>

## Voice fingerprint (0-1 scales)
- Funny vs serious: <0-1>
- Formal vs casual: <0-1>
- Respectful vs irreverent: <0-1>
- Enthusiastic vs matter-of-fact: <0-1>

## Readability target
- Audience tier: <general | professional>
- Flesch Grade: <e.g. 8-11>
- Read-aloud test: if a sentence sounds like a brochure, rewrite it.

## Voice signature (non-negotiable)
- <one distinctive rule, e.g. one opinionated expert judgment per article>
- <one honest admission of limitation per article>
- <soft close only — the CTA style>
